-- The modifier chain (w3): modifiers stack forward through a multicast onto its first bolt. Twin of 123-modifier-chain.bqn. (was w3-modifier-chain)
-- Modifiers ride forward: with every modifier ahead of every bolt, both Damage Plus land on the block's first projectile, and the binding collapses to one scoped fold.
-- Wand [DP, DP, Triple, SB, SB, SB]: one cast block (the Triple's +3 keeps the balance alive to the end); both Damage Plus ride to the first member projectile — the correlated "next projectile after each modifier" join is the .bqn's reverse min-scan; here every modifier precedes every bolt, so the target collapses to the block's first projectile, one scoped fold.
-- The damage write is one barrier: the target selection is a fold-in-predicate (min/ over the member projectiles), the stack size a counted mask.
--! registry ../registries/123-modifier-chain.reg
--! expect bal = 0 1 1 3 2 1 0
--! expect minBal = 0 1 1 1 1 1 0
--! expect member = 0 1 1 1 1 1 1
--! expect damage = 0 0 0 0 23 3 3

Spell , Bal = 1 + (+\ (DrawAdd - 1) @ Spell)
Spell , MinBal = 0 - (max\ (0 - Bal) @ Spell)
Spell @ deck & (Slot == 0 | prev.MinBal > 0) , +Member
Spell & Proj & Member & Slot == min/ Slot @ (Spell & Proj & Member) , Damage += 10 * (#/ (Spell & Mod & Member))
